      "type": "harness fault-injection race",
      "observed": "Output is precreated before Transformer initializes its muxer. Waiting only for existence lets injected sparse growth be truncated by actual writer initialization; the long movie completes successfully instead of observing the intended byte ceiling.",
      "repair": "Require >1024 actual bytes plus MP4 ftyp before injecting sparse growth. Require the real watchdog to settle within5 seconds, with unchanged256MiB rejection, cleanup and writer-release assertions."
    },
    {
      "type": "production per-page frame loss masked by earlier dimension failure",
      "observed": "Three one-second still pages have87 frames, below unchanged88..92 acceptance. The slow-video page has133333us gap at3866667->4000000, above unchanged120000us maximum.",
      "sourceBasis": "Pinned default frame-dropping program keeps the preceding frame, then releases it without forwarding at each end-of-input. VideoGraphInput supplies effect-adjusted cumulative offsets; speed effect scales only delta from each first timestamp.",
      "repair": "Memory-only pass-through limiter shared across per-page shader programs, after speed. It forwards real frames separated by>=33333us, has no final lookahead texture, and fails if input timestamps run backwards. Story renderer behavior unchanged."
    }
